        },
        {
          "document_id": "01a013b8ae5b739fa6c9ed188153c01a",
          "score": 0.5309386849403381,
          "text": "Rathold Rátót\nRathold (I) from the kindred Rátót (Hungarian: Rátót nembeli (I.) Rátót (Ratolt)) was a Hungarian distinguished nobleman from the gens Rátót, who served as ispán (comes) of Somogy County in 1203.He was the eldest son of voivode Leustach Rátót. As his brother, Julius I Rátót had no successors, Rathold was the ancestor of the Gyulafi branch of the Rátót clan.",
