        {
          "document_id": "01a013c21f407a838ee5273beb5f0834",
          "score": 0.701620876789093,
          "text": "Ann Carver's Profession\nAnn Carver's Profession is an American pre-Code 1933 film directed by Edward Buzzell. It focuses on the relationship of a female lawyer and her husband, and on the strain that her financial success places on their marriage. The film stars actress Fay Wray and this film was made during the year she cemented her fame in King Kong. Although the writing credits differ, the film bears a striking resemblance in plot to Columbia's 1938 production The Lady Objects starring Lanny Ross and Gloria Stuart.",
          "source_hops": [
            0
          ]
        },
        {
          "document_id": "01a013c21f6c7f28ab28a5ccadd5a891",
          "score": 0.6230669021606445,
          "text": "Ann Carver's Profession\nPlot",
          "source_hops": [
            0
