        },
        {
          "document_id": "01a013c3cc307d1589e053f5601d45a0",
          "score": 0.6430572867393494,
          "text": "Keōpūolani\nThis lineage gave her unquestionable social and political influence, which made her a coveted marriage partner for a chief to ensure heirs to inherit the combined ranks and birthrights of both parents. She married Kamehameha in 1795 and their marriage linked the House of Kamehameha to the ruling house of Maui and the old ruling house of Hawaii. Although Kamehameha had his own claims to these island, Keōpūolani further cemented his legitimacy over his usurpation of his cousin, Keōpūolani's father.",
          "source_hops": [
            0
