          ]
        },
        {
          "document_id": "01a013c5140f7175aa95ac0799aedd12",
          "score": 0.5659369826316833,
          "text": "Et moi, et moi, et moi\nWords by Jacques Lanzmann and music by Jacques Dutronc.",
          "source_hops": [
            0
          ]
        },
        {
          "document_id": "01a013c514ab7db39d84654820c52151",
          "score": 0.5643508434295654,
          "text": "Et moi, et moi, et moi\n\"Mini, mini, mini\" – 1:54",
          "source_hops": [
            0
          ]
        },
        {
          "document_id": "01a013c5132a7efcbf793d3af07f90c0",
          "score": 0.5563643574714661,
          "text": "Et moi, et moi, et moi\n\"Et moi, et moi, et moi\" was released as the lead track on a four-track EP (EPL. 8461) by Vogue in France in August 1966. In the UK and The Netherlands, it was released as a 2-track 7\" single, with \"Mini, mini, mini\" as the b-side. In Germany, \"Mini, mini, mini\" was released as an a-side, backed with \"Et moi, et moi, et moi\". For the Italian market, an Italian-language version titled \"Il Mundo Va Cosi\" was recorded. A version in Japanese was also attempted but was not released.Dutronc performed \"Et moi, et moi, et moi\" on the French television show Le palmarès des chansons, broadcast on Channel One by the Office de Radiodiffusion Télévision Française on 29 September 1966. He also toured to promote the single.",
