        {
          "document_id": "01a013ccd59574b88767f69ad5beeaa9",
          "score": 0.577126681804657,
          "text": "Carrie Watson Fleming\nHer husband, Aretas Fleming, served as Governor of West Virginia from 1890-1893. After a shortened three year term as first lady, due to the controversial 1888 election, the Flemings returned to Fairmont, where she played a prominent role in Fairmont's cultural, civic, and religious activities.",
