          "document_id": "01a013ce01a37e92a57fe36d8ada4b74",
          "score": 0.6460468769073486,
          "text": "Trịnh Doanh\nTrịnh Doanh (4 December 1720 – 15 February 1767) ruled northern Vietnam (Tonkin) from 1740 to 1767 (he ruled with the title Minh Đô Vương). Trịnh Doanh was the third son of Trịnh Cương, and belonged to the line of Trịnh lords who ruled northern Vietnam. His rule was spent putting down rebellions against Trịnh rule.",
          "source_hops": [
            0
          ]
        },
        {
