        },
        {
          "document_id": "01a0177fbc467e498dd39161598b1ad1",
          "score": 0.498632550239563,
          "text": "Francisco Giner de los Ríos\nJ.B. Trend: The Origins of Modern Spain. New York: The Macmillan Company 1934.",
          "source_hops": [
            0
          ]
        },
        {
          "document_id": "01a0177fbc8971958ef2eb3eeab13652",
          "score": 0.4943477511405945,
          "text": "Francisco Giner de los Ríos\nFrancisco Giner de los Ríos. Polymath Virtual Library, Fundación Ignacio Larramendi",
          "source_hops": [
            0
          ]
        },
        {
          "document_id": "01a0177ffe5971fc8fc971e6983e78c8",
          "score": 0.4941958487033844,
          "text": "Taifa of Jaén\nThe Taifa of Jaén (Arabic: طائفة جيان) was a medieval Islamic taifa Moorish kingdom centered in Al-Andalus. It existed for only two very short periods: first in 1145 and then in 1168. It was ruled by Arabs of the Banu Khazraj tribe. The Taifa was centred in the present day region of Jaén in southern Spain.",
          "source_hops": [
            0
          ]
        },
        {
          "document_id": "01a0177fbbe678f2a007c392aa567417",
          "score": 0.4866052269935608,
          "text": "Francisco Giner de los Ríos\nGiner continued his work outside the university, even after he was reinstated in his university chair in 1881. Among the many important people who were at one time or another associated with the Institución Libre de Enseñanza and the related Residencia de Estudiantes were José Ortega y Gasset, Federico García Lorca, Salvador Dalí, Antonio Machado, Luis Buñuel and Miguel de Unamuno.",
          "source_hops": [
            0
          ]
        },
        {
          "document_id": "01a0177fbbcb7a2ab1943ac91715b628",
          "score": 0.4820292592048645,
          "text": "Francisco Giner de los Ríos\nHe openly criticized the government for its attempts to stifle academic freedom. As a consequence, in 1875, he lost his chair at the university, which led to what can be seen as his major achievement: the 1876 foundation of the Institución Libre de Enseñanza (Institute of Free Teaching), a private school of higher learning. He dedicated his life to the formation of human beings along coeducation; rationalism; and freedom of teaching, research, and literary communication. The goal was a society in which free citizens would be governed by free citizens on the basis of an adequate education. Because of his \"rational realist\" approach to law, he can also be seen as one of the forerunners of the sociology of law.",
          "source_hops": [
            0
          ]
        }
