          "document_id": "01a017995b3075d4b63ce1d561106388",
          "score": 0.6586116552352905,
          "text": "Starship Command\nAcornsoft's Starship Command is a multidirectional shooter released in 1983 for the BBC Micro and Acorn Electron. It was available on cassette as well as 5.25\" disc for the BBC and ROM cartridge for the Acorn Electron Plus 1 expansion module. The game was written by Peter Irvin who, along with Jeremy Smith, went on to create the arcade adventure Exile.",
