        {
          "document_id": "01a013f46fee7377b5e5a9708305158d",
          "score": 0.7026137113571167,
          "text": "Mika Häkkinen\nMika Pauli Häkkinen (Finnish: [ˈmikɑ ˈhækːinen] (listen); born 28 September 1968), nicknamed \"The Flying Finn\", is a Finnish former racing driver. He won the Formula One World Drivers' Championship in 1998 and 1999, both times driving for McLaren. Häkkinen is one of three Formula One drivers from Finland that have won the World Drivers' Championship, and the only one to have done so more than once. He currently works in driver management and is a brand ambassador for various companies.",
