          "text": "Sand Lake, New York\nAs of the census of 2010, there were  8,530 people, 3,009 households, and 2,229 families residing in the town.  The population density was 226.9 inhabitants per square mile (87.6/km2).  There were 3,277 housing units at an average density of 93.1 per square mile (35.9/km2).  The racial makeup of the town was 96.4% Non Hispanic White, 0.4% African American, 0.11% Native American, 0.50% Asian and 1.1% from two or more races. Hispanic or Latino origin were 1.5% of the population. Ancestries: German (25.2%), Irish (22.6%), English (14.6%), Italian (13.8%), French (8.9%), Polish (6.1%).",
