        },
        {
          "document_id": "01a014040a327d31a218ec1f98377abe",
          "score": 0.6249698400497437,
          "text": "Celtic nations\nFormerly Gaulish regions",
          "source_hops": [
            0
          ]
        },
        {
          "document_id": "01a01404271878b494d84269d21c238c",
          "score": 0.6179976463317871,
          "text": "Continental Celtic languages\nUse of term",
          "source_hops": [
            0
          ]
        },
        {
          "document_id": "01a0140409c2743f8b95a3a5df05fbee",
          "score": 0.6179912090301514,
          "text": "Celtic nations\nModern-day Galicians, Asturians, Cantabrians and northern Portuguese claim a Celtic heritage or identity. Despite the extinction of Iberian Celtic languages in Roman times, Celtic heritage is attested in toponymics and language substratum, ancient texts, folklore and music.",
