          "text": "Baraki Barak District\nDistricts of Afghanistan",
          "source_hops": [
            0
          ]
        },
        {
          "document_id": "01a014191ac276a2b7f0202f06cae326",
          "score": 0.5484312772750854,
          "text": "Baraki Rajan\nBaraki Rajan (Dari/Pashtun: برکی راجان) is a town within the Baraki Barak District of Logar Province, Afghanistan. Baraki Rajan lies approximately 3 km south of the town of Baraki Barak, the capital of the Baraki Barak District. Baraki Rajan is the location of the largest bazaar in the Baraki Barak District, with over 1,200 shops and businesses, with a 50+ bed hospital near the town center, making Baraki Rajan an important center for commerce within the District.",
          "source_hops": [
            0
          ]
        },
        {
          "document_id": "01a01418e86176629c3805f65ba6c12f",
          "score": 0.5390183329582214,
          "text": "Baraki Barak District",
          "source_hops": [
