          "score": 0.6114931106567383,
          "text": "Frederick John Fulton\nFrederick John Fulton, KC (December 8, 1862 – July 25, 1936) was a  British-born and educated Canadian lawyer and politician.  He practiced law in Kamloops, British Columbia.  He was a member of the British Columbia Legislative Assembly from 1900 to 1909 serving a series of cabinet roles as President of the Executive Council, Minister of Education, Provincial Secretary, Attorney General and Chief Commissioner of Lands and Works.  As Attorney General, he prosecuted and convicted the notorious Bill Miner.",
